ed claims from this functional probe.\nFor auto stats verify old OFF lab limitation, explicit existing sync\/async\/lowpriority\/compat\/state capture, plain unfiltered COUNT only, actual plan\/OptimizerStatsUsage vs namedstats timestamps\/modcounter\/rows before\/after, bounded cumulative observation windows and async\/XE limitations. No universal COUNT triggers\/never triggers claim and no production blanket flag toggles. For operational bridge examine blank plus FILLED independent restored copy and dedicated replica examples, explicit fictional illustrative_not_measured data not recommended thresholds, shared CPU\/memory\/storage\/device\/network\/primary effects, actual caps mechanism verification or HOLD, metric source\/privileges\/unavailable not0, normal variability, detection\/aggregate\/delivery\/decision\/cancel\/rollback\/jitter upper budget vs measured time-to-risk not conversion from p99msdelta, recovery\/owner and pending-arrival SLO accounting. MySQL MDL\/undo\/applier + SQL request\/TX\/version\/PVS\/AG primary recovery concrete observations. Ordinary COUNT no rowlock does not mean zero MDL; no new intentional contention injection. Do not insist on full performance grid or real network partition experiment where guide explicitly defers all unverified cases safely. Request experiment only indispensable to a current operative claim; doc correction is sufficient when it removes that claim.\nFirst form independent findings. Then read results\/reviews\/issue-1\/final-engineer-result.json and assess its findings in independentFindingAssessment.\nReturn concise JSON accepted(bool), decision accepted\/rejected, documentHashes exact current 4doc hashes, findings with stableid\/severity high|middle|low and concrete scenario\/fix, requestedExperiments, reviewQuestions {betterMethods,designCoverage,omissions,lockFactors,fastCount}, coverageReport mapping Issue1 items1-4 to evidence\/pass or fail, reviewEvidence paths\/hashes\/observations. No high\/middle or indispensable experiment may remain at acceptance. Aggregate acceptance.json pending until both reviews finish; do not require prior accepted receipt. Do not waive defects. Low optional improvements can remain if no unsafe recommendation.\n\nExact inputs: {\"documents\": {\"docs\/guidelines\/mysql.md\": \"ffb3ae5b8d189b90418c9fb9efa8e5d2787c2bcae328a60e9c3fedcf907c2b2f\", \"docs\/guidelines\/sql-server.md\": \"bbfdada6f71acc91010c8457c076cae1b79d00e6aac07247ff6f66ec547ff47c\", \"docs\/README.md\": \"9783f53da8b3e4613628d3f6798d7f5753cbcf9be3a7fadd9e6b7c67c27c48a3\", \"docs\/guidelines\/operations-runbook.md\": \"27ae9f91f863acb759abf913459755f502108af33c4524650e214ce1e2cf73d1\"}, \"baselineSha256\": \"f35110a6fab261ab7021c8f2e4f7976b6f888f18c311446bd09b5387c78b2f1e\", \"issueSha256\": \"5f94a59773fec11f737812e7f69d105e2b5bbf7c33e51638b607451779fbe3b9\", \"ownerProofSha256\": \"56a995a783884baa76a0194d4a53ebc63b3855f10b402751fdf3e4168f3654f8\", \"ownerAuditSha256\": \"d50ff3cb01b3fdb00dd1d5ae88aca2b340f5deef1e37c5d6f2fa14ebccad5ee3\", \"runtimeArchiveManifestSha256\": \"f8e81e1e1d4adc9ba7a0d6fffe8e2eeafd4e12231ec59cb12b6dab3a74daeef6\", \"sourceHashes\": {\"sqlserver\/issue1\/lab.rb\": \"7401978cd34d13111e8a763c457cce4ba972885ce7de0b6b0c3615f8260cc437\", \"sqlserver\/issue1\/mise.toml\": \"9200d44b709fb4266977ad0eea81e11a56849d716c14e901706fe946f8092e4c\", \"sqlserver\/issue1\/compose.yaml\": \"1826cfb7e8ac74f869b93c4415e039357ebe224f389d3faa9c43f9fc12f27b3a\", \"sqlserver\/issue1\/Dockerfile\": \"fc330088772578d04b795cd5630ddebe7c58c0ff4e3b74f9e8acf0b58bdd5f90\", \"sqlserver\/issue1\/.dockerignore\": \"f4a08bffb3077b9356083081520f9987342a4988dd06574763311c2b776417d4\", \"sqlserver\/issue1\/CountIssue1.csproj\": \"e63af41a60a9e3ceb49db23c993e00f37128cab8e6b4cc25df61a6d52f8c2de0\", \"sqlserver\/issue1\/NuGet.Config\": \"fd6836e883aa6bf334e587a02ff7239f68713f4baac6d749f743a2b489b1769c\", \"sqlserver\/issue1\/packages.lock.json\": \"9f4ed17378bdc9695074f16496aa31c416c7ef22